%% Payment recovery and courier integration boundaries
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Scheduler
    participant Callback as Provider callback
    participant API as NestJS API
    participant Queue as Recovery/courier queue
    participant Worker as Tenant-stamped processor
    participant Provider as Payment or courier adapter
    participant DB as Tenant PostgreSQL
    participant Notify as Notification/audit work

    alt Expired prepaid attempt
        Scheduler->>Queue: Enqueue tenant organizationId + attemptId
        Queue->>Worker: Deliver recovery job
        Worker->>DB: Serializable claim of payment attempt
        alt Claim already handled
            DB-->>Worker: No-op current state
        else Claim succeeds
            Worker->>Provider: Reconcile or expire attempt
            Provider-->>Worker: Verified provider state
            Worker->>DB: Idempotently update payment/order state
            Worker->>Notify: Record outcome and side effects
        end
    else Courier webhook
        Callback->>API: Raw body + signature + tenant callback token
        API->>API: Verify authenticity and store callback evidence
        API->>Queue: Enqueue normalized tenant job
        Queue->>Worker: Process callback
        Worker->>Provider: Normalize provider status if needed
        Worker->>DB: Update shipment/order event transactionally
        Worker->>Notify: Schedule customer/admin notification
    else Courier polling
        Scheduler->>Queue: Fan out READY/ACTIVE organizations
        Queue->>Worker: Deliver organization-scoped poll job
        Worker->>Provider: Poll outside DB transaction
        Provider-->>Worker: Shipment status or timeout
        Worker->>DB: Persist event, attempt, and normalized status
    end

    Note over Worker,Provider: Provider calls stay outside database transactions.
    Note over Queue,Notify: Timeouts use bounded retries and dead-letter evidence; one provider outage must not block other tenants.
